  "label": "John McCain is mapped as the speaker of the sarcastic apology",
  "description": "The text 'sorry, trump...' is overlaid on John McCain's image, implying that he is the one apologizing to Trump. His smiling expression is used to convey sarcastic or mocking humor, projecting the persona of a speaker delivering the text. The visual material (John McCain) is mapped onto the textual material (the apology) to create the illusion that he is the source of the statement.",
